arkets agree at 80% or better for Shah. Feely's fundraising and outside-spending advantage, plus a mildly damaging headline for Shah, justify trimming the expected margin somewhat below what the ratings consensus alone implies.", "watch": "Feely's cash advantage and the outside-spending wave against Shah could close the gap if he consolidates Republican voters while the Libertarian draws a few points from Shah.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: David Schweikert (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Arizona's 1st District is an open seat with Republican incumbent David Schweikert running for governor instead. Amish Shah, a state lawmaker who beat the Democratic establishment in the primary, faces former NFL kicker and broadcaster Jay Feely, with Libertarian Monica Alponte also on the ballot. The district leans slightly Republican on paper, but most expert raters call it a Democratic flip, and prediction markets price Shah's chances at 80% or higher.\n\nFeely has out-raised Shah and holds a large cash-on-hand edge, and outside groups have spent heavily against Shah while leaving Feely unopposed on the air. A single Democratic-sponsored poll from last fall showed the race essentially tied, and recent coverage highlights both the competitiveness of the seat and a stumble by Shah over a claimed endorsement from a party that does not exist.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7982, "margin": 5.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7812, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7872, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7849, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7435, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7308, "margin": 4.9}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7977, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8149, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.799, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-